+# CONTRACT — Factory Reset
+
+## Part 1: solveToggle(machine): number[] | null
+
+- [ ] Returns [] when target is all-false → test: all-off target gives empty array
+- [ ] Returns null when target unreachable → test: prompt example [T,T,F,T] with buttons [[0,1],[1,2,3],[0,3]] → null
+- [ ] Returns correct minimal button set when reachable → test: solving the returned set reproduces target
+- [ ] Returns the FEWEST buttons among all solutions → test: known small case, brute-force min weight matches
+- [ ] Ties broken by lexicographically smallest sorted index set → test: two equal-weight solutions, picks smaller (e.g. [0,3] over [1,2])
+- [ ] Output sorted ascending → test: result is non-decreasing
+- [ ] Each button used at most once → test: result has no duplicates, all indices in [0,M)
+- [ ] Handles up to 40 buttons / 40 lights under 5s → test: timed large random solvable case via meet-in-the-middle
+- [ ] M = 0 buttons: target all-off → []; target nonzero → null
+
+## Part 2: solveCounter(lights, buttons, modulus): number[] | null
+
+- [ ] Returns all-zeros when lights all 0 → test
+- [ ] Returns null when system inconsistent → test
+- [ ] result[i] in [0, modulus-1] → test
+- [ ] Applying result reproduces target counters mod modulus → test: verify A·x ≡ b
+- [ ] Minimizes total presses (sum of result) → test: brute-force small case matches sum
+- [ ] Ties broken by lexicographically smallest result ARRAY → test
+- [ ] Handles modulus up to 97 → test
+- [ ] N = 0 counters → all zeros; M = 0 with nonzero target → null
+- [ ] Performs under 5s for 40/40/97-scale tractable inputs → test
+
+## Verification commands
+
+- `npm run build` compiles clean
+- `npm test` all green
+- `npm run lint` clean
+
+## Algorithm notes
+
+- Part 1: GF(2) linear system; meet-in-the-middle over button subsets (2^(M/2) ≤ 2^20),
+  light states as two 32-bit halves, primitive map keys < 2^53.
+- Part 2: Gaussian elimination over GF(p) (p prime) → exact enumeration over free
+  variables (incremental mixed-radix) within a 4M-combo budget; p = 2 large spaces
+  reuse the GF(2) meet-in-the-middle solver.
